article.en:
The Kính Thiên hall (Vietnamese: Điện Kính Thiên;  
chữ Hán:  敬天殿) was the throne hall built as the central structure of the imperial palace complex of the Later Lê dynasty, located in its capital Đông Kinh (present-day Hanoi). The palace hall was renamed Long Thiên Palace (Vietnamese: Điện Long Thiên;  
chữ Hán:  隆天殿) in 1841 during the reign of Emperor Thiệu Trị of the Nguyễn dynasty.
